# Credentials never live in this repository. It is published to GitHub Pages, so
# anything committed here is public the moment it is pushed. The sprite pipeline
# reads its keys from the environment; the file they are kept in lives outside
# the working tree entirely (~/.config/gamo/secrets.env, mode 600).
#
# These patterns are a backstop, not the mechanism. If a key ends up matching one
# of them inside the repo, something has already gone wrong upstream of here.
.env
.env.*
*.secrets.env
secrets.env
**/api_key*

# Python bytecode from the sprite tools.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Maven build output for the side-server. The jar is built inside Docker.
server/target/

# The generated cutscene panels at full size: seven 3 MB PNGs that nothing
# reads after build_cutscene.py has cut them. The masters are the WebPs in
# motorio/assets/cutscene, the prompts are in tools/sprite/gen_cutscene.py, and
# the per-call sidecars beside these are committed.
motorio/tools/sprite/cutscene/*.png
motorio/tools/sprite/cutscene/*.png.import
